   9 | fn example(x: Bytes) -> Holder {
     |               ^^^^^ provided: `x` is a borrowed parameter; it lives in the caller's region
 --> ../../conformance/CLO/CLO-4-stored-borrowed-capture-bad.hir:11:13
  11 |     action: fn() {
     |             ^^^^^^ required: an escaping closure owns its captures, which must be immutable, owned and global (CLO-4)
  = help: 1. declare the parameter `take x` (no cost; callers write `take x`, which moves their value into this call)
  = help: 2. `unique x` (deep copy: allocates, costs O(size), and is not allowed under `@noalloc`)
  = note: `copy x` does not help: a copy shares the blocks of `x`, which stay local
error[MODE-7]: this use needs an owned value; write `copy` to share it: the value is local, but this needs an owned value
 --> ../../conformance/CLO/CLO-4-stored-borrowed-capture-bad.hir:12:15
  12 |       let _ = x
     |               ^ 
 --> ../../conformance/CLO/CLO-4-stored-borrowed-capture-bad.hir:12:15
